WEBVTT

00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:15.875
[sighs]

00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:19.625
[players clamoring]

00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:23.125
[players cheering]

00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:27.166
[Valentina] Riley!

00:00:28.666 --> 00:00:31.291
[♪ uplifting music playing]

00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:12.458
[Sofia] Yes!

00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:14.208
[player] Whoo!

00:01:14.291 --> 00:01:15.291
[players laughing]

00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:34.583
-[indistinct chatter]
-[all laughing]

00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:35.666
Hey, Minnesota,

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.000
how long are you gonna
stare at your phone?

00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:38.458
It's almost 2:00.

00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:40.250
Coach is gonna post
the list any minute.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.666
-Okay. 2:00 p.m. That's in...
-Six minutes.

00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:44.125
And what happens if we don't
become a Fire Hawk?

00:01:44.291 --> 00:01:46.750
Well, thanks for asking, Joy.
I'll tell you.

00:01:47.375 --> 00:01:49.000
First, Mom and Dad
are very disappointed.

00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:50.083
We don't go pro,

00:01:50.166 --> 00:01:51.250
and we find work
as an ethnomusicologist...

00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:52.458
even though we don't
really know what that is.

00:01:52.541 --> 00:01:54.875
We have no friends,
and we die alone.

00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:56.250
-[screams]
-Okay, okay.

00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:58.166
None of that
is happening right now.

00:01:58.333 --> 00:01:59.333
-Is it?
-No.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.416
Great! So why don't we take
a seat in our special chair.

00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:05.041
Yeah, that's a great idea.
[sighs in relief]

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.500
See? Isn't that better?

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.000
[distorted] Oh, yeah,
that's the stuff.

00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:11.250
We can't control whether Riley
makes the team.

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:12.875
But what can we control?

00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:14.333
-Well, um... Oh!
-[cup clattering]

00:02:14.416 --> 00:02:16.541
Riley has a Spanish test
tomorrow. We need to study.

00:02:16.625 --> 00:02:17.625
Oh! You're right.

00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:18.833
-We totally...
-Olvidamos!

00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:20.375
-What's that mean?
-"Forgot."

00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:21.583
[Fear] Someone paid attention
in class.

00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:22.666
[Disgust] I never would've
thought of that.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:23.750
-You're clearly an expert.
-[Envy] Muchas gracias.

00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:24.833
Oh, thanks, guys.

00:02:24.916 --> 00:02:26.041
Plus, we followed our new

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:28.333
varsity caliber
training program.

00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:29.708
Oh, I wish I thought of that.

00:02:29.875 --> 00:02:31.333
Newsflash, you did!

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.291
Wait, you're right, I did.
[chuckles]

00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:35.625
I'm jealous of myself.
Thanks for the reminder.

00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:36.958
[male voice] You're welcome!

00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:39.375
-Who said that?
-It's my new buddy, Pouchy.

00:02:39.541 --> 00:02:41.416
Hi, everybody. I'm Pouchy!

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.166
Confetti if we make the team!

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.458
-Good idea. Ah!
-[party horn blows]

00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:47.458
That's great, but either way,
we love our girl.

00:02:47.541 --> 00:02:48.875
Confetti if we don't!

00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:50.166
-[party horn blows]
-[Fear coughs]

00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:51.625
-[phone vibrates]
-[gasps]

00:02:51.708 --> 00:02:53.416
Oh, is it Coach's email?

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.833
No. It's Bree and Grace.
[chuckles]

00:02:55.958 --> 00:02:58.208
Aw. I miss those girls.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.000
Oh. Remember when
Bree and Grace,

00:03:01.083 --> 00:03:02.416
-and us used to...
-You're still early.

00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:03.958
-No, no, no. Too early.
-Go downstairs.

00:03:04.125 --> 00:03:06.625
I'll just be downstairs
if you need me.

00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:08.250
[Joy] It's 3 minutes to 2:00.

00:03:08.416 --> 00:03:10.875
-She's got this.
-'Cause she's got us.

00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:16.375
Ooh, yeah! Right? 'Cause
she's... [nervously] Maybe?

00:03:16.541 --> 00:03:18.041
All right, Embarrassment.

00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:20.041
Everybody,
look at Embarrassment!

00:03:20.916 --> 00:03:22.166
[whimpers]

00:03:22.416 --> 00:03:24.333
Hey, look, if you don't
make it this year,

00:03:24.416 --> 00:03:25.541
there's always next year.

00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:27.125
I know.

00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.625
-I love our girl.
-How could you not?

00:03:29.791 --> 00:03:31.208
She's super smart.

00:03:31.291 --> 00:03:32.750
[Sadness] And great at hockey.

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:34.125
[Disgust]
She's really creative.

00:03:34.291 --> 00:03:36.666
She can be bored,
but never boring.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.458
But she can be a little
sarcastic from time to time.

00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:42.541
[Fear] She can have
really bad ideas.

00:03:42.708 --> 00:03:45.416
[Anger] Occasionally, she can
do the wrong thing.

00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:48.625
[Joy] And sometimes, she can be
too hard on herself.

00:03:48.958 --> 00:03:51.708
But every bit of Riley
makes her who she is.

00:03:52.416 --> 00:03:54.625
And we love all of our girl.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.833
Every messy,
beautiful piece of her.

00:03:59.958 --> 00:04:00.958
-[phone vibrates]
-[gasps]

00:04:05.375 --> 00:04:07.541
[♪ hopeful music ends]

00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:13.833
[♪ upbeat music playing]

00:04:28.791 --> 00:04:31.083
So, Riley, how was camp?

00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:34.833
Okay, we talked about this.
We tell them everything.

00:04:34.916 --> 00:04:36.208
Uh...

00:04:36.291 --> 00:04:37.291
But what about sneaking

00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:38.541
-into Coach's office?
-What about hitting Grace?

00:04:38.625 --> 00:04:39.625
-Remember the lying?
-Are we gonna

00:04:39.708 --> 00:04:40.750
tell her about the Fire Hawks?

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:42.250
-She doesn't need to know.
-Objection.

00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:43.416
Pardon. Excusez moi.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:44.625
[console chimes]

00:04:44.708 --> 00:04:45.708
It was good.

00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:51.041
She goes away for three days
and all we get is, "good"?

00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:52.250
And what about
the red in her hair?

00:04:52.416 --> 00:04:53.416
Did she join a gang?

00:04:53.583 --> 00:04:55.041
Welcome back, Anxiety.

00:04:56.916 --> 00:05:00.541
She goes away for three days
and all we get is, "good"?

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:03.500
Yeah. Sounds right.
Back to the game.

00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:05.541
[commentator] With a nice pass
over to Reeves,

00:05:05.625 --> 00:05:07.166
comes across center ice.

00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:09.750
Down to the line.
Oh, what a move!

00:05:09.833 --> 00:05:11.958
[♪ upbeat music continues]

00:06:48.083 --> 00:06:50.083
[♪ mysterious music playing]

